Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• "USERS"."created_at": restrict registrations to 01‑Jan‑2019 – 30‑Apr‑2022  
• "USERS"."age": identify each customer’s age, locate the maximum (oldest) and minimum (youngest) values, and count how many users share those values  
• "USERS"."id": optional primary key to aggregate / join if you want to double‑check counts  
• (Only if you want to cross‑reference orders) "ORDERS"."user_id" & "ORDERS"."created_at": validate that the user really placed an order inside the period, though not needed for the requested statistic  

Typical date‑window condition you will reuse  
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 /*2019‑01‑01*/  
                        AND 1651276800000000 /*2022‑04‑30*/  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 each) that move from very simple checks to the final computation path.  
All column names are enclosed in double quotes and every query is accompanied by a brief comment.

```sql
-- Description: Quick peek at raw user registration timestamps and ages
SELECT "id", "created_at", "age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Distinct ages present in the whole USERS table (sanity check)
SELECT DISTINCT "age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
ORDER BY "age" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Sample 20 users registered inside the required date window
SELECT "id", "created_at", "age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Identify the oldest age among users in the window (one value)
SELECT MAX("age") AS "oldest_age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Identify the youngest age among users in the window (one value)
SELECT MIN("age") AS "youngest_age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Count how many users have the oldest age value obtained above
SELECT "age", COUNT(*) AS "num_oldest_users"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
  AND "age" = (SELECT MAX("age")
               FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
               WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000)
GROUP BY "age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Count how many users have the youngest age value obtained above
SELECT "age", COUNT(*) AS "num_youngest_users"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
  AND "age" = (SELECT MIN("age")
               FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
               WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000)
GROUP BY "age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Show both oldest and youngest counts together for clarity
WITH limits AS (
  SELECT MAX("age") AS max_age,
         MIN("age") AS min_age
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
  WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
)
SELECT u."age",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_users"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS" u
JOIN limits l
  ON u."age" IN (l.max_age, l.min_age)
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
GROUP BY u."age"
ORDER BY u."age" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Produce one row containing both counts side by side
WITH age_extremes AS (
  SELECT MAX("age") AS oldest_age,
         MIN("age") AS youngest_age
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
  WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
),
counts AS (
  SELECT
    CASE
      WHEN "age" = (SELECT oldest_age FROM age_extremes) THEN 'oldest'
      WHEN "age" = (SELECT youngest_age FROM age_extremes) THEN 'youngest'
    END AS age_group,
    COUNT(*) AS num_users
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
  WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
    AND "age" IN ((SELECT oldest_age FROM age_extremes),
                  (SELECT youngest_age FROM age_extremes))
  GROUP BY age_group
)
SELECT *
FROM counts
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Compute the numerical difference between the two counts
WITH age_extremes AS (
  SELECT MAX("age") AS oldest_age,
         MIN("age") AS youngest_age
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
  WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
),
counts AS (
  SELECT
    CASE
      WHEN "age" = (SELECT oldest_age FROM age_extremes) THEN 'oldest'
      ELSE 'youngest'
    END AS grp,
    COUNT(*) AS cnt
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."USERS"
  WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651276800000000
    AND "age" IN ((SELECT oldest_age FROM age_extremes),
                  (SELECT youngest_age FROM age_extremes))
  GROUP BY grp
)
SELECT ABS(MAX(CASE WHEN grp = 'oldest'   THEN cnt END) -
           MAX(CASE WHEN grp = 'youngest' THEN cnt END)) AS diff_between_oldest_and_youngest
FROM counts
LIMIT 20;
```

